#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:5
#: 1a5c16463f964c2e8679759b94aa6bcd
msgid "Tips for Improving QuadPlane Safe Operation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:7
#: f3108708b325483b9ae9d0e827058394
msgid "Large commercial QuadPlanes not only represent significant investments, but also can have safety concerns due to their size and speed. Often these vehicles are operated near their operational limits to obtain maximum duration and payload delivery. Here are some tips to prevent accidents, based on reported incidents and subsequent analysis by ArduPilot support engineers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:9
#: 893e3b809e0a4d1e8a3c2551cff84151
msgid "Utilize an autopilot with redundant IMUs and sensors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:10
#: 7d2bcdcba5ed4647acac73eaa915f303
msgid "Utilize a quality airspeed sensor, compass, and GPS. Redundant sensors are suggested, if possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:11
#: 15d08b7589c64ba29df6e1f2da380675
msgid "Read and follow the Wiki's :ref:`plane-configuration-landing-page` and :ref:`quadplane-setup` instructions. Be sure to setup the :ref:`Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX<Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MAX>` and :ref:`Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN<Q_M_BAT_VOLT_MIN>` parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:12
#: 1af3553da49a41d094cba4c2c3dc2e63
msgid "Follow the Wiki's :ref:`quadplane-vtol-tuning-process` instructions before the first hovers. In step 10, using the QuickTune LUA script is preferable to manual TX tuning, or using the AUTOTUNE mode. Be sure to :ref:`autocal the airspeed sensor<calibrating-an-airspeed-sensor>` in the first Fixed Wing flight and follow the :ref:`Fixed Wing Tuning<tuning-quickstart>` and subsequent tuning pages' instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:13
#: feff26729c5345be94fd32e120de4682
msgid "After the first VTOL/FW/VTOL flights, use MAVExplorer's MAGFIT utility to refine the :ref:`compass calibration <common-magfit>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:16
#: 3cacfa2d0eb942e18bedd7fa60ffe966
msgid "Suggested Parameters (differing from defaults)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:18
#: 5868ba94f81b4e4091e99cd1d51d7578
msgid "Although it requires setup per flying location, the use of :ref:`DO_LAND_START<common-do-land-start>` missions and :ref:`RTL_AUTOLAND<RTL_AUTOLAND>` is advised, to control approach direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:19
#: 67a014af0a144eb882c170a2b71a8c6d
msgid "Be sure to configure the landing sequence with long enough base and final legs so as to assure the turn offshoots are corrected before the final transition to VTOL on landing. A vehicle moving at 30m/s with 30deg maximum bank angle will only turn at 9 deg/sec resulting a >200meter turn radius. Bear in mind that winds can widen the turn radius significantly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:20
#: 1e034e99eeec4f0bb8e79c39dc6988b6
msgid "Be sure to set the :ref:`TECS_LAND_ARSPD<TECS_LAND_ARSPD>` parameter, it should be set to just above :ref:`AIRSPEED_MIN<AIRSPEED_MIN>`, which should be 25% above stall speed, otherwise the normal cruise airspeed will be used on the approach, greatly increasing the radius of turns and their recovery to the mission path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:21
#: 243243341c6e4bcb851dd4e6fe682e41
msgid "Test the above landing sequence in SITL with the -f quadplane frame, using your parameters for TECS, and pitch/roll angle limits, to assure it can execute the landing pattern correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:22
#: e7803ab66c374831b72e70a40cccb872
msgid "Use :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>`, bit 5 = 1 to assure that RC failsafes while in VTOL modes are treated as QRTLs instead of QLANDs, if not operating on a mission with :ref:`DO_LAND_START<common-do-land-start>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:23
#: 5773560c55524700a101d470a0c08234
msgid "Set :ref:`Q_ASSIST_SPEED<Q_ASSIST_SPEED>` to be about 3m/s less than :ref:`AIRSPEED_MIN<AIRSPEED_MIN>`, but still above the vehicles stall speed, to avoid undesired assist operation within the normal operating speed envelope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:24
#: dced3cc6c8a5497dabcf73c93006ccf2
msgid "Set the transition failure timer :ref:`Q_TRANS_FAIL<Q_TRANS_FAIL>` to an appropriate time and set :ref:`Q_TRANS_FAIL_ACT<Q_TRANS_FAIL_ACT>` to QRTL, unless operating at BVLOS distances. In this case, it might be better to set the action to warning only and decide what do as the situation warrants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-reliability.rst:25
#: fbd3d4b991b44a96b44430a77d5bb94f
msgid "When setting up the Battery Failsafe, use :ref:`BATT_FS_LOW_ACT<BATT_FS_LOW_ACT>` = 6 for a fixed wing return, loiter down to :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>`, and QLAND."
msgstr ""
